WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to talk
about Donald Trump

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.770 size:88% position:44%
because in 2011 I hosted

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
the White House
Correspondents´ Dinner.

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:06.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-I told some jokes about him.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that year,
you actually emceed --

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:11.811
people forget this happened
very, like, soon before.

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:13.680
You did the Comedy Central
"Roast of Donald Trump"...

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:14.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s right.
-...when you emceed it.

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:16.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he actually seemed to be
a pretty good sport.

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:19.352
Certainly a better sport there
than he was a few months later.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:20.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
What was your memory
of that night?

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:22.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I -- you know,
the strange thing was,

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:23.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
I-I have the same thought,
like he´s --

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:25.025 size:75% position:38%
he´s taken all this.

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:26.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
The only thing I think we
weren´t allowed to joke about

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:29.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
was the bankruptcy.
-Yeah.

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:30.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Bankruptcies.
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Everything else was kind of
on the table.

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:36.836
That was the one thing he was
sensitive about. And I just --

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:38.638 size:84% position:42%
-I guess that´s the one
that goes the farthest

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:40.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
against what he
presents himself as.

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:42.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah. Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:43.843
-But I just remember thinking,

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:46.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
"man, this guy is really
freaking boring."

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:47.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:48.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is...
-Like, in your interactions

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:49.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
with him?
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:50.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It´s like this guy´s just

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:52.118
really dull and it´s -- it´s --
it´s, you know,

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:55.055
I meet -- businessmen at that
level that I´ve met in the past,

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.556
it´s kind of the same reaction.
It´s like they´re just --

00:00:56.556 --> 00:01:00.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
they just seem like dull guys.
-Yeah. And dull guys --

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And unfortunately, yeah.
-Dull guys don´t make

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:04.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
for great roast -- ´cause they
actually, they finished.

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:06.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
They closed the night.
-Yeah.

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:08.568
I mean, every joke that -- that
we told, you know, it´s like,

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:12.172
hey, Donald Trump...you know,
I don´t know what the hell

00:01:12.172 --> 00:01:14.941
the joke was, when he has sex,
he closes his eyes and imagines

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:16.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
himself jerking off.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:20.513
And I look over -- and that joke
and every -- I look over

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Trump´s face is like...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:25.885
It´s like -- kind of like, "all
right, I´ll give him that one."

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:29.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So -- so not the same guy

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:31.124 size:88% position:44%
that he seems to be now.

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:33.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, he´s -- he´s turned --
he´s evolved?

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:36.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:37.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So...
-Yeah.

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:39.699
-Congratulations, "Family Guy´s"
16th season.

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:40.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-That´s amazing.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:44.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:46.673
-And, you know, it´s everywhere.
-Yep, yep, yep.

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:48.641
-The show is everywhere,
multiple countries and --

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.977
which is nice and easy when you
have an animated show,

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:52.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
´cause you just have people
re-record...

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-...in their language.

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:55.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
But are there jokes
that you make

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:58.118 size:78% position:39%
that do not translate
into other languages?

00:01:58.118 --> 00:01:59.786
-I -- there -- there have to be.
-Yeah.

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:02.922
-There have to be. The show has
weird titles elsewhere.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:05.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was told that in Korea
the show is called,

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:07.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The Shocking Family."
-Oh, well...

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:08.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-That´s the title of the show.

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:12.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I like that they were worried
that people would see it

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
as, like, guidance if they
didn´t call it that.

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:16.002
-Yeah, exactly --
-Like this is a regular family.

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:17.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, so I don´t know.
I don´t know.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.639
And that kind of gives
everything away up front.

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:22.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you ever get to hear --
like, do they run by,

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:24.744 size:81% position:41%
"hey, here´s the voice
of the person in Korea

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:26.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
who´s going to do
the characters"?

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:30.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, they -- they...
[ Laughs ] they don´t.

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:31.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-They don´t.

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:32.852
And I -- I don´t -- you know,
like every once in a while,

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:34.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´ll catch a clip of,
like, "Family Guy" or "Ted"

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:36.122
in German and it´s like Peter,

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:40.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
but he´s like...
[ Imitating German ]

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And it´s like, that wow --

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:44.030
that -- I don´t know what´s
going on. I don´t know how

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:46.566
the show is perceived there.
-Do you -- when you hear it,

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:48.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you have an appreciation
where you say,

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:49.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
"that´s a pretty good
German Peter"?

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:52.038
-I´m just glad somebody else is
worrying about it.

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:55.775
-Yeah, that´s -- I liked. Yeah.
Micromanaging, that is --

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:57.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
that´s a loser´s game.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:57.544 --> 00:03:00.780
-You -- these characters, these
voices, do you just sort of,

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, talk until you find
something you like

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:04.050
or are they based on people?

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:06.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, it´s -- they come
from different places.

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:07.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, Stewie, as I´ve said
in the past,

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:09.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
is based on Rex Harrison.
-Mm-hmm.

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:12.058
-He´s the character actor
from those Henry Higgins.

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:14.093
Peter was based on a
security guard that I went to --

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:16.529
you know, worked at my college,

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:17.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the Rhode Island
School of Design.

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:19.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Does he know this?

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:21.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think he -- I -- they don´t
know which one,

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I´ve never kind of made
it clear which one.

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:25.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-There´s a very specific guy,

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:29.209
but they all -- there´s actually
several of them, you know,

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:31.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
are like, "oh, yeah,
that´s me he´s talking about."

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:32.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:35.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And do you think -- do you
think when he says that

00:03:35.515 --> 00:03:38.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
and people hear it, they go,
"oh, it <i>is </i>you"?

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:40.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you think it -- is it that
close to him

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:41.721 size:81% position:41%
that they would say --

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:43.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It´s -- it´s -- yeah, yeah,
it´s possible.

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:44.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]
-You know what?

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:46.593
They´re a lovely bunch of guys,
if I can make them all happy

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:47.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
believing
that they´re all Peter.

00:03:47.961 --> 00:03:50.063
-[ Laughs ] That´s true.
-Then that makes me happy.

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:53.233
-And so obviously you were
a Rhode Island School of Design

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:55.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
artist before anything else.
Pretty much, right?

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:59.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah, I was --
-And you -- I was hearing that

00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:03.343
your first cartoon actually got
you in trouble, which sort of --

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:05.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
certainly trends towards
a guy who makes a show called

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:06.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The Shocking Family."
-Yes, yes.

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:09.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What was your early cartoon
and your early complaint?

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:12.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Shockingly, I-I-I wanted to
work for Disney

00:04:12.118 --> 00:04:13.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I was at the --
in college...

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:14.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
...if you can believe that.

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:15.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And then that --

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:17.557 size:78% position:39%
-That would have been
a whole different --

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:18.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That went away.
-Yeah.

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:21.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And... [ Laughs ]
-Yeah.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:24.063
-And, no, I got a-a hate letter
from the town priest

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:25.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
for doing a --

00:04:25.465 --> 00:04:26.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:29.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Can it be a hate letter
from a --

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:33.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I don´t know. You know,
listen, I was doing comics

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:34.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a local paper.
I was 10-years-old,

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:37.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
getting a letter from
a priest -- wait a second.

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:39.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Um...

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:44.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hang on. It just -- the --
you know, I was 10.

00:04:44.651 --> 00:04:47.453
The cartoon was a guy getting
communion at church and he says,

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:49.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
"can I have fries with that?"
You know?

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:50.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-10-years-old.

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:52.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
-10-years-old,
that´s such a very --

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:53.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-That´s a really good, edgy,

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:55.461 size:75% position:38%
10-year-old joke....
-Sure, absolutely.

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:57.797
-...that anybody 14 or over
should not be offended by it.

00:04:57.797 --> 00:05:01.734
-Yeah, no, it´s fine. It´s fine.

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:03.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
You might see it
in "Family Circus."

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:05.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But, yeah, the letter said,

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:07.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
"shame on you for insulting
the Almighty God

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:09.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
and those who love Him."
-Wow!

00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:11.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
-That sounds like a priest who

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:13.746
<i>has </i>been asked a few times,
"can I have fries with this?"

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:15.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah.
-Exactly.

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:17.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
And from that point on,
I knew exactly

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:19.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
what I wanted to do
with my life.

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:22.722 size:84% position:42%
-And when -- how far,
like, were you still --

00:05:22.722 --> 00:05:25.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
Disney was actually when
you were at RISD?

00:05:25.058 --> 00:05:27.360
-At college, yeah, yeah.
-And like when did you realize,

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:29.262 size:88% position:44%
"oh, this isn´t gonna --
I shouldn´t do Disney."

00:05:29.262 --> 00:05:31.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know -- it was two-fold.
I started doing stand-up.

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:33.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-And was getting laughs

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:35.435
with a certain type of material,
and I thought,

00:05:35.435 --> 00:05:37.070
"well, that -- this isn´t going
to fly there."

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:38.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And then "The Simpsons"

00:05:38.338 --> 00:05:40.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
obviously reinvented
the whole ball game and --

00:05:40.373 --> 00:05:41.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Oh, God, you can --

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:43.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
cartoons are once again
not just for kids,

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:45.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
so it was two-fold.

